⍝ Helper for `dyalog FILE.apla`: read an array-notation file and display it.
⍝ Usage (inside the container): dyalogscript show-apla.apls /app/Grid.apla
⍝ In array notation a line break means the same as ⋄, so joining the lines
⍝ with ⋄ and evaluating gives the array.
args←2⎕NQ'.' 'GetCommandLineArgs'
:If 2>≢args ⋄ ⎕←'usage: show-apla.apls FILE.apla' ⋄ ⎕OFF 2 ⋄ :EndIf
file←2⊃args
⍝ Drop ⍝ comments (but not a ⍝ inside quotes) and blank lines first,
⍝ otherwise one comment would swallow the rest of the joined text.
NoComment←{(∧\~(⍵='⍝')>≠\⍵='''')/⍵}
lines←NoComment¨⊃⎕NGET file 1
lines←(∨/¨' '≠lines)/lines
a←⍎¯3↓∊lines,¨⊂' ⋄ '
⎕←file,': rank ',(⍕≢⍴a),', shape ',(⍕⍴a),', depth ',⍕≡a
⎕←a
⍝ Namespaces only display as #.[Namespace], so also show their contents
:If ∨/'#.[Namespace]'⍷∊⍕a
    ⎕←'as JSON:'
    ⎕←1(⎕JSON⍠('HighRank' 'Split')('Compact' 0))a
:EndIf
